{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3c5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a18347-a386-7071-8a7b-e45ab0a366f1"},"sequence":61,"recorded_at":1780531400000117,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"01a18347-a539-7003-a92b-84861f36de97","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"command_id":"01a18347-a539-7003-a92b-84861f36de97","event":{"chunk":"Read text file `RESCUE_LOG.md`.\n1|# Rescue log\n2|\n3|Code changes not written by Muse Code. Each has a `Rescue:` commit.\n4|\n5|| Date (UTC-3) | Task | File | Change | Why not Muse |\n6|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n7|| 2026-10-27 | 05 | app/player.tsx | `handleEnded` ignores an element that ends while a fade runs | Found in the live browser check after merge. The loop crossfade starts 3 s before the end, so the outgoing element ends as the fade finishes; it was still marked audible and started a second loop fade, restarting the track. One-line guard; task 05 had used both Muse review rounds. |\n8|| 2026-10-28 | 24 | server/images/env.ts | Blank cap values fall back to the default instead of a zero cap | Muse review round 1 finding; two-line guard after the single allowed round. |\n9|| 2026-10-28 | 25 | core/music-session.ts | Previous resolves history through the audible scope, not the current style | Muse review round 1: style scoping changed Previous after a style switch; restoring old behaviour while keeping the playlist-only fix. |\n10|| 2026-10-28 | 24 cleaning | core/fixtures/clean/*.json | Trimmed EPUB section fixtures extracted from Gutenberg/Standard Ebooks samples by the research script | Data extracted by a script, not code; Muse wrote all cleaning code |","final_result":true,"kind":"output","task_id":"01a18347-b99f-7141-be34-4bf26a24b539"},"kind":"task_lifecycle","run_stream":{"id":"01a18347-a539-7003-a92b-84861f36de97","kind":"run"},"task_id":"01a18347-b99f-7141-be34-4bf26a24b539","task_stream":{"id":"01a18347-b99f-7141-be34-4bf